    description: "STATEMENT: entry.file_name() on a std::fs::DirEntry is not bound to the repository's one file_name. OBSERVED at e948d2ae3 on diesel: of the 14 calls the name step bound that had no bind of that name before, 5 right and 9 wrong (Path::file_name, Command::stdout / stderr / args); of the 1,549 it restored to their earlier target, 13 right of 15 read (wrong: String::as_str, slice::first). SUPPRESSED_METHOD_NAMES means no stub at all and feeds a disclosure, so these names need another home: a stub with stdlib_member_name. Also open in rust.py: tuple-struct and enum-variant constructors called by imported name; a wildcard of another file's inline module (use diesel::dsl::*); #[cfg] alternatives counted as several holders.\n\nEvidence and method: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/pilot_11252026/DESIGN.md and final/ (maps mine_e948 at e948d2ae3 against before/ at dev 0d3c12ff4; hand samples seed 20261125). Found during the ADR-0064 pilot (rust, csharp, javascript/typescript); not built there because fewer than two of the three pilot languages need it, or because it is the analyzer's own."  # 853e
