  message: "Two additions from the pilot's last measurements (2026-11-26, branch jgstern-agent/feat/shared-call-resolution-pilot).\n1. A call inside a macro body can lose its edge and leave NO stub. aardvark-dns src/dns/coredns.rs:99, `tokio::spawn(Self::process_tcp_stream(self.inner.clone(), sock, addr));` inside `tokio::select!`: bound to CoreDns::process_tcp_stream before the adapter, neither bound nor reported now. On the three pilot trees 276 of the 2,409 lost Rust calls have no stub at the call site. The macro-body route itself was left as it was (it still looks names up among everything: 931 `name` edges of Rust origin); what changed for this site was not traced.\n2. Fixed in the pilot, recorded here because it is the same family: a call that names its owner made a stub even when the name is one the analyzer declines to model and the owner is the prelude's (`Vec::new()`, `Box::new(x)`): 413 stubs on the three trees, withheld again (02667a6e1), with the stub kept when the file's table binds the owner's head to the tree (3c1edb9e7: `select_by::SelectBy::new()` after `mod select_by;`)."  # 06bf
